# The STarKos player and its song SK10, the intro tune of Zynaps 2 in 1 ($8000-$90C4, 4293 bytes,
# work/parts/starkos-8000.bin; the intro copies it from block 1's $D810 to $8000 and runs it there): the single
# source of truth for src/sound/starkos*.asm (tools/part_mkasm.py; the format: kit/mkgame.py, class Annotations).
#
# Witnesses: the L1 of the intro window of c1 (work/stage2/intro/l1.json, frames 2182-2838: Init once, Play 566
# times, the first three patterns: the run counts quoted below); a SkoolKit simulation of the player from its
# loaded image (tools/sound_render.py): after Init and 385 Play calls its 4293 bytes equal the recording's page 2 at
# frame 2600 (work/images/intro-title-bank2.bin, $8000-$90C4) at every byte; the song's format by
# tools/sk10.py check (the text src/res/music/sk10.txt gives the 1845 bytes back).
#
# The player is self-modifying: nearly all of its variables are the operands of its own instructions (LD A,n /
# CP n / LD HL,nn / LD DE,nn / OR A or SCF). A label names the instruction; the variable is Label+1 (or +2, +3).
# Their loaded values are in the image, Init sets the ones a song needs.

@module starkos-play ; the entries and the line: speed, patterns, the special track, the three tracks
@about The intro (block 1, docs/03-build-and-load.md 3.4) calls PlayerEntries with DE = Song ($6061), then PlayerPlay from its IM 2 handler once a frame ($60DF), and jumps to PlayerStop when it ends ($60BA). On a 48K ($5D3B = 0) none of them runs.
@about A STarKos song is a list of patterns. Each pattern has a height (lines), three tracks (the linker: one track address a channel), a transposition per track and a special track (speed changes and digidrums). The three per-pattern values come from run-length streams, each read once a pattern: the transpositions (TranspPointer), the heights (HeightPointer) and the special tracks (SpecialListPointer); the linker (LinkerPointer) gives three words a pattern. The song's last pattern ends where the special list begins (LinkerEnd); the four streams then restart at the song's loop points. The song's bytes and the format: src/res/music/README.md, tools/sk10.py.
@about Play runs one frame: SpeedCounter counts up to Speed; on the frame it reaches it, a new line: at a pattern's first line (NewPatternFlag = SCF) the streams and the linker give the pattern, then the special track and the three tracks are read (each track's wait counts down the empty lines), LineCounter counts the pattern's lines. Every frame then goes on at PlayInstruments (starkos-frame.asm) for the sound of the three channels.
$8000 c PlayerEntries ; the jump table: Init ($8000), Play ($8003), Stop ($8006)
> $8000 JP Init (input DE = the song: $8990); $8003 JP Play; $8006 JP Stop. In c1: Init once, at the intro's start; Play 566 times in the intro window (one a frame); Stop once, when the intro ends.
$8003 PlayerPlay ; JP Play
$8006 PlayerStop ; JP Stop
$8009 w PlayerOrigin 1 ; $8000: the address the player was built for
> No instruction of the player or of the intro reads it.
$800B b DigidrumNumber ; the digidrum the song asked for this frame (0: none)
> Zeroed by Play each frame, set by a special track's drum line or a track's drum command; for the host to play a sample. The intro never reads it (no reference in block 1's code), and SK10 has no drum (sk10.txt).
$800C b DigidrumChannel ; the channel (1-3) of that digidrum
> A track's drum command sets its channel number; a special track's drum line sets the song's drum channel (header byte 6, copied to SpecialDrum+4 by Init).
$800D c Play ; one frame of the song: a line when the speed count ends, then the instruments
> No input; changes every register (the intro's handler saves them). DigidrumNumber = 0, Retrigger = 0 (the R13 retrigger flag); SpeedCounter + 1 until it equals Speed, else 0 and a new line (NextLine). 566 runs in the intro window, 95 of them a new line (Speed 5: six frames a line).
$800E ; no digidrum this frame
$8011 ; no envelope retrigger yet this frame
$8014 SpeedCounter ; SpeedCounter+1: the frames of this line so far
$8016 Speed ; Speed+1: the frames a line - 1 (the song's speed, its special track's speed lines)
$801A ; not yet: count, and only the instruments this frame
$8021 NextLine ; a new line
$8025 NewPatternFlag ; OR A ($B7): the pattern goes on; SCF ($37): a new pattern at this line
$8029 ; a new pattern: the three tracks' waits 0
$8032 ; the next lines are not the pattern's first
$8037 TranspWait ; TranspWait+1: patterns left with the same transpositions
$803D TranspPointer ; TranspPointer+1: the transposition stream
$8042 ; bit 0: a hold (the count in bits 1-7)
$8046 ; bits 1-5: track A's transposition (5 bits signed), bit 7: track B's byte follows, bit 6: track C's
$804F TranspSetA ; into TrackAInstrument+2 (D, added to each note)
$8052 ; bit 7 of the byte
$8058 ; track B's transposition byte
