@module starkos-frame ; every frame: the three instruments, the track and instrument line formats
@about PlayInstruments runs every frame after Play's line work. For each channel (A, B, C: three copies of the same code) it adds the track's pitch slide to the pitch sum, sets LinePitch, IXL = the note and IY = the channel's tone register in SendRegisters' cache, and calls InstrumentLine with HL = the instrument's line and A = the instrument's frame counter. InstrumentLine writes the channel's period, volume (and noise, envelope) into the cache and returns IXH = the channel's mixer bits (bit 0 tone off, bit 3 noise off). The counter then runs up to the instrument's speed; at it the next line, and at the instrument's end its loop address (a looping instrument) or instrument 0's silent line with speed 255 (a one-shot). The three mixer pairs make R7 and SendRegisters (starkos-output.asm) sends what changed.
@about ReadTrackLine is the track format (a note, a note with volume / instrument / slide, a wait, a rest to the pattern's end, volume, slide, off, a digidrum) and InstrumentLine the instrument line format (the volume, arpeggio, pitch, noise, a fixed period, the hardware envelope with its period from the tone's or the tone's from the envelope's). Both are in tools/sk10.py's docstring with the byte layout; the text src/res/music/sk10.txt writes each line in those terms.
$82B0 c PlayInstruments ; every frame: the instruments of channels A, B, C, the mixer, then SendRegisters
> HL' = Retrigger (the instruments' hardware lines OR their retrigger bit into it), D' = the channel's attenuation. Per channel: PitchSum += Slide; LinePitch = PitchSum; InstrumentLine(HL = the instrument line, A = the counter, IXL = the note, IY = the channel's period cache); then the counter: below Speed + 1, the same line next frame; at it, the next line (InstrPointer = the line's end), or at InstrEnd the loop. Ends in JP SendRegisters with A = R7 (IXH of C, B, A: A's bits 0 and 3, B's 1 and 4, C's 2 and 5). 566 runs.
$82B3 ChanAAtten ; ChanAAtten+1: track A's attenuation, subtracted from every instrument volume
$82B6 ChanAPitch ; ChanAPitch+1: the pitch sum (the slides of the frames so far)
$82B9 ChanASlide ; ChanASlide+1: the track's slide a frame
$82C0 ; LinePitch: half of it is added to the period
$82C8 ChanAInstrPointer ; ChanAInstrPointer+1: the instrument's line
$82CB ; IY = AYReg0+1: channel A's period low byte (+$1B the high byte, +$36 the volume)
$82CF ; A = the counter: InstrumentLine retriggers the envelope at 0 only
$82D5 ; DE = the line's end
$82D6 ChanAInstrCounter ; ChanAInstrCounter+1: frames of this line so far
$82D8 ChanAInstrSpeed ; ChanAInstrSpeed+1: the instrument's speed (frames a line - 1; 255 holds)
$82DC ; not yet
$82DF ChanAInstrEnd ; ChanAInstrEnd+1: the instrument's end
$82E7 ChanAInstrLoop ; ChanAInstrLoop+1: its loop address
$82EA ChanAInstrLoops ; OR A: a one-shot, SCF: it loops
$82ED ChanAZeroEnd ; ChanAZeroEnd+1: instrument 0's end (Init): a one-shot ends in instrument 0's line
$82F3 ; the speed 255: that line holds
$82F8 ChanANextLine ; the next line
